    {
      "slide": 3,
      "pptx_slide": 3,
      "title": "Genomics 101",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "Genomics 101",
        "DNAs and RNAs determine who",
        "and what we are.",
        "They contain the instructions that",
        "guide the formation, functioning,",
        "and regulation of every cell.",
        "Ultimately shaping our physical",
        "characteristics, health, and even",
        "aspects of our behavior."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "f61a5288092de61a93fc2be7089f30a5c51b40cc6f4d6a6c366e7d1c61a16adb"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 4,
      "pptx_slide": 4,
      "title": "DNAs",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "DNAs",
        "• Cells are categorized into",
        "Eukaryotic and Prokaryotic cells.",
        "• In Eukaryotic cells, DNAs are “packaged”",
        "to form chromosomes.",
        "• Mitochondria also has",
        "a circular chromosome."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "b04790138dced9d42ed91fed04aec01741ec45d5ce2c5e49f0851c3bacdfd537",
        "ed16c3f69b34f7ea0a475d374ffa6c3b719ec479b97e27cfb766f950473f712b",
        "460ff63f0da119f9151983e7bfff381498104078bcdc342d3f6876364c5f3716"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 5,
      "pptx_slide": 5,
      "title": "From DNAs to RNAs",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "From DNAs to RNAs",
        "DNAs affect human through gene expression:",
        "• DNA instructions are transcribed into RNA.",
        "• Messenger RNA (mRNA) carries these",
        "instructions from DNA to ribosomes, where",
        "proteins are synthesized.",
        "• Proteins synthesized from RNA instructions",
        "determine physical characteristics, such as eye",
        "color, height, and hair texture."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "7b1a0336df83e377f8e9a5d7bcd92e8941fff97d4bf97191216f6c154d1bce50"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 6,
      "pptx_slide": 6,
      "title": "How to Obtain Data?",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "How to Obtain Data?",
        "RNA sequencing is a ubiquitous",
        "tool in biomedical research for",
        "measuring gene expression in a",
        "population of cells.",
        "To measure gene expression, match",
        "short reads back to the reference",
        "genome or transcriptome (known",
        "RNA sequences), and count the",
        "number to measure expression",
        "levels."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "10a36a7e0285c390346b04b49de81758afac5bd7fe86e9ce149fdea6180aff11"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 7,
      "pptx_slide": 7,
      "title": "How to Obtain Data?",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "How to Obtain Data?",
        "Whole genome sequencing can be used to",
        "recover the whole DNA sequence.",
        "• The very first human genome was completed in",
        "2003 as part of the Human Genome Project.",
        "• Today, sequencing technology is much more",
        "efficient, and a human genome can be",
        "sequenced in a matter of days for under",
        "$10,000."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "383bd2bb870488c39810236b873c19edd22d7a7cbc5833acbed2e5b83089ae8a"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 8,
      "pptx_slide": 8,
      "title": "How to Obtain Data?",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "How to Obtain Data?",
        "Assay for Transposase-Accessible Chromatin",
        "using sequencing (ATAC-seq) is used for",
        "assessing genome-wide chromatin",
        "accessibility.",
        "• Varies between different cell types and even",
        "among cells of the same type under different",
        "conditions or developmental stages."
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "afdcd25a7e079d0db02d5d4227a7812d58756c5525c9a3b5d0ce2b2635fe5508"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    {
      "slide": 9,
      "pptx_slide": 9,
      "title": "Bonus: How to Obtain 3D Data?",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "pending",
      "text": [
        "Bonus: How to Obtain 3D Data?",
        "Three representative methods (also used for proteins):",
        "• X-ray Crystallography",
        "• Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) Spectroscopy",
        "• Cryogenic Electron Microscopy (Cryo-EM)"
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "b984a3cd93e4110a2e6f3a99df7b6f1e0fd4aed5aeda624c0eeb8937c11b26be",
